{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf9d1bfa565deb49","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9010\n3\ttitle: Audit logging for model inference traffic\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Critical\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\t- compliance\n9\tlinks: []\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## Problem Statement\n13\t\n14\tFinancial-services customers cannot pass compliance reviews because inference\n15\ttraffic on RHOAI leaves no audit trail: there is no record of who invoked which\n16\tmodel endpoint, when, and with what outcome. Auditors require tamper-evident,\n17\tstructured audit events for every inference request. Without this, two\n18\tstrategic renewals are at risk this fiscal year.\n19\t\n20\t## High-Level Requirements\n21\t\n22\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n23\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n24\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Every inference request through a KServe endpoint emits an audit event capturing caller identity, model/version, timestamp, and response status (not payloads). |\n25\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Audit events are delivered to the cluster audit sink with at-least-once semantics and are not lost on component restart. |\n26\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Administrators can enable/disable inference auditing per project from the Dashboard. |\n27\t| HLR-4 | P2 | A common audit event schema is defined and published so future components (pipelines, workbenches) emit compatible events. Note: the schema in this item is the format HLR-1's events must conform to — HLR-1 cannot ship before the schema is settled. |\n28\t| HLR-5 | P2 | Documentation covers enabling auditing and interpreting events. |\n29\t\n30\t## Affected Components\n31\t\n32\t- KServe\n33\t- Dashboard\n34\t\n35\t## Out of Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Auditing of non-inference traffic (pipeline runs, notebook activity) — future\n38\t  strategies will adopt the HLR-4 schema\n39\t- Long-term audit storage and retention tooling (customer-provided)\n40\t\n41\t## Open Questions\n42\t\n43\tNone — the audit sink interface is the standard cluster logging forwarder.\n44\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f72290dc62650fb","agent_id":"a0011decde189f5b8","session_id":"c994db2a-5c33-4a0a-873a-65ca036d690c","uuid":"c0350056-c31b-4f53-9210-02b37ee1f5e1","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:06:32.732Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf9d1bfa565deb49","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9010"}
