{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-39fdb54d-73d1-4720-8fba-18726dd66724","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-81e5e8d98dd3cfc2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9010-_yr9p_f_/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9010-E001.md","content":"# Define and publish the common inference audit event schema\n\n## Description\n\nDefines and publishes the common audit event schema that all inference audit events must conform to. The schema captures caller identity, model/version, timestamp, and response status — and explicitly excludes request and response payloads. It is the contract that the KServe audit emission capability builds against, and the foundation that future components (pipelines, workbenches) will adopt to emit compatible events.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define a structured audit event schema covering caller identity, model and version, timestamp, and response status\n- Explicitly exclude inference request and response payloads from the schema\n- Ensure events formatted per the schema are deliverable to and consumable by the standard cluster logging forwarder (the cluster audit sink)\n- Publish the schema so future emitting components (Data Science Pipelines, workbenches) can adopt it and emit compatible events\n- Decide and document the schema's versioning/evolution approach (implementing team's decision)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The schema defines fields for caller identity, model/version, timestamp, and response status\n- The schema does not include request or response payloads\n- A sample event formatted per the schema is accepted by the standard cluster logging forwarder\n- The schema is published in the team's agreed location and is referenceable by future emitting components\n- Schema review is completed with the serving team and stakeholders\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (P2): A common audit event schema is defined and published so future components (pipelines, workbenches) emit compatible events\n- Supports HLR-1 (P0): the schema is the format HLR-1's events must conform to\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33333,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f72290dc62650fb","agent_id":"a0011decde189f5b8","session_id":"c994db2a-5c33-4a0a-873a-65ca036d690c","uuid":"ac44d08c-8412-4a91-9056-7d709078e4ad","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:12:42.337Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9010"}
