{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-434d121f-f99f-431f-94de-c9dbed8b7172","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-942ed240d9675cd9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9010-_yr9p_f_/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9010-E003.md","content":"# Dashboard administration control for per-project inference auditing\n\n## Description\n\nAdds an administrative control in the RHOAI Dashboard that enables administrators to enable and disable inference auditing per project. The control writes the per-project audit configuration surface defined and honored by the serving-side audit emission capability; the Dashboard itself owns no data plane and acts through Kubernetes CRs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Project-level administration surface for toggling inference auditing per project (placement consistent with existing Dashboard settings patterns is the implementing team's decision)\n- Write the per-project audit setting through the configuration surface the serving side honors (Dashboard reads and writes Kubernetes CRs)\n- Restrict the control to project administrators via OpenShift OAuth project-scoped RBAC\n- Reflect the current audit-enabled state accurately in the project view\n- Unit and integration tests for the control and RBAC behavior\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- An administrator can enable and disable inference auditing for a project from the Dashboard\n- The setting persists and is reflected accurately when the view is reloaded\n- Non-administrator users cannot change the audit setting\n- Toggling the control changes the serving side's behavior: audit events are emitted when auditing is enabled and none are emitted when disabled\n- The change passes the existing Dashboard build pipeline\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): Administrators can enable/disable inference auditing per project from the Dashboard\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_rea