R captures tamper-evidence (e.g., integrity protection of the event stream); the HLRs only require structured events with at-least-once delivery. If auditors require cryptographic tamper-evidence, that is additional scope not covered by any HLR — flag to the strategy author. It would extend the emission epic's scope, not change epic structure.\n70\t3. **Docs epic priority derivation:** E004 is P0 by the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy priority Critical) even though HLR-5 is P2. This is by design; flagged for reviewer awareness.\n71\t4. **Unaddressed NFR:** HLR-2's \"not lost on component restart\" implies durable local buffering in the serving path; the latency/performance impact on inference traffic is not addressed by any NFR (none exist). Captured as an acceptance criterion on E002.\n72\t\n73\t## Tiered Delivery\n74\t\n75\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing. The audit sink is the standard cluster logging forwarder (in-platform), and no upstream contributions or third-party coordination are required.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8cf8bb8dc4ea8fe9","agent_id":"a2feb364de901ae31","session_id":"c994db2a-5c33-4a0a-873a-65ca036d690c","uuid":"d23e6809-f82a-49f0-bc0f-77d6565a0bba","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:15:14.595Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aee0706e9f9b4411","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review decomposition RHAISTRAT-9010"}
