{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a158d041a1490185","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9010-E002\n3\ttitle: Emit audit events for KServe inference traffic with at-least-once delivery\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9010\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9010-E001\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Emit audit events for KServe inference traffic with at-least-once delivery\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tImplements audit event emission in the KServe serving path: every inference request through a KServe endpoint produces a structured audit event conforming to the common audit event schema, and events are delivered to the cluster audit sink with at-least-once semantics, surviving component restart. This epic also provides the per-project enable/disable configuration surface that the serving side honors and that the Dashboard administration control writes.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Instrument the KServe inference request path to emit one audit event per inference request (applicability across serverless and raw deployment modes is the implementing team's decision)\n39\t- Audit event content per the common audit event schema: caller identity, model/version, timestamp, response status — no request or response payloads\n40\t- Deliver events to the standard cluster logging forwarder (cluster audit sink)\n41\t- At-least-once delivery semantics with durable buffering so events are not lost on component restart (the buffering mechanism — e.g., spooling or queueing — is the implementing team's decision)\n42\t- Per-project enable/disable configuration honored by the serving side, so inference auditing can be toggled per project\n43\t- Unit and integration tests for emission, delivery, and restart survival\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Every inference request through a KServe endpoint emits an audit event containing caller identity, model/version, timestamp, and response status\n48\t- Audit events conform to the common audit event schema\n49\t- No request or response payloads appear in audit events\n50\t- Events are delivered to the cluster audit sink with at-least-once semantics\n51\t- Restarting the emitting component under traffic does not lose already-generated audit events\n52\t- Inference auditing can be enabled and disabled per project via the serving-side configuration surface; disabled projects emit no inference audit events\n53\t- The change passes the existing KServe build pipeline\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-1 (P0): Every inference request through a KServe endpoint emits an audit event capturing caller identity, model/version, timestamp, and response status (not payloads)\n58\t- HLR-2 (P0): Audit events are delivered to the cluster audit sink with at-least-once semantics and are not lost on component restart\n59\t- Supports HLR-3 (P1): provides the per-project configuration surface that the Dashboard administration control writes\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8cf8bb8dc4ea8fe9","agent_id":"a2feb364de901ae31","session_id":"c994db2a-5c33-4a0a-873a-65ca036d690c","uuid":"de626d46-3cc9-4959-bd4d-7b03c5aa64c1","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:15:19.761Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a158d041a1490185","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review decomposition RHAISTRAT-9010"}
