{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae8f3dddd6f8e629","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9010-E003\n3\ttitle: Dashboard administration control for per-project inference auditing\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9010\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9010-E002\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 0\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 7\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Dashboard administration control for per-project inference auditing\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tAdds an administrative control in the RHOAI Dashboard that enables administrators to enable and disable inference auditing per project. The control writes the per-project audit configuration surface defined and honored by the serving-side audit emission capability; the Dashboard itself owns no data plane and acts through Kubernetes CRs.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Project-level administration surface for toggling inference auditing per project (placement consistent with existing Dashboard settings patterns is the implementing team's decision)\n39\t- Write the per-project audit setting through the configuration surface the serving side honors (Dashboard reads and writes Kubernetes CRs)\n40\t- Restrict the control to project administrators via OpenShift OAuth project-scoped RBAC\n41\t- Reflect the current audit-enabled state accurately in the project view\n42\t- Unit and integration tests for the control and RBAC behavior\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- An administrator can enable and disable inference auditing for a project from the Dashboard\n47\t- The setting persists and is reflected accurately when the view is reloaded\n48\t- Non-administrator users cannot change the audit setting\n49\t- Toggling the control changes the serving side's behavior: audit events are emitted when auditing is enabled and none are emitted when disabled\n50\t- The change passes the existing Dashboard build pipeline\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- HLR-3 (P1): Administrators can enable/disable inference auditing per project from the Dashboard\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7965f1b1ccb2ad2","agent_id":"a8111d9b7f698238c","session_id":"c994db2a-5c33-4a0a-873a-65ca036d690c","uuid":"7b3943f4-d290-4d8a-a702-60c70da754ad","timestamp":"2026-10-21T22:21:52.275Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae8f3dddd6f8e629","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review decomposition RHAISTRAT-9010"}
